jobs.description:
Can your colleagues in production count on spotless and hygienic workspaces? Do you enjoy staying active on the job? Then you can quickly start working as a cleaner or industrial cleaner at Luiten! Your full-time workday starts around 9:00 or 10:00 AM. You’ll change into your work attire, grab your cleaning materials and equipment, and begin moving between the various production areas with your high-pressure cleaner.
Not only will you thoroughly clean the production spaces, but you’ll also ensure that the machines used to process and package meat—and all related materials—are meticulously cleaned. You take care of your own work, following HACCP and hygiene regulations carefully. In addition to cleaning, you make sure that every area is safe to enter and ready for use.
No need for an activity tracker here, as you’ll definitely get plenty of daily movement in this role! Together with your friendly, multicultural team, you’ll ensure production can start on time and in a clean environment.

- You are available full-time from Monday till Friday;
- Overtime doesn’t wear you out—instead, it makes your wallet fuller;
- You speak Dutch or English, essential for safety on the work floor;
- Some experience with cleaning and/or sanitation is a plus.

Are you a real hands-on person who enjoys staying physically active? We are looking for a Warehouse Employee to join the team of a family-owned company in the meat industry. You will work in a refrigerated environment and mainly be responsible for picking and moving meat products.

It is important that you are comfortable working in cold temperatures. To keep you properly protected, you will be provided with a warm jacket, trousers and gloves.

What will you do?

As a Warehouse Employee, you and your colleagues will make sure that orders are prepared correctly and on time. You will work with various meat products and stay physically active throughout your shift.

Your responsibilities will include:

- Picking meat products based on customer orders;
- Picking and preparing orders for shipment;
- Moving crates containing meat products;
- Lifting crates weighing up to approximately 20 kg;
- Checking products and quantities;
- Keeping the warehouse clean, tidy and organized;
- Supporting colleagues with various warehouse activities;
- Handling products carefully and following applicable hygiene regulations.

You will be working in a refrigerated environment, so you must be comfortable working in the cold throughout your shift. To help you work comfortably and safely, you will receive protective clothing, including a warm jacket, trousers and gloves.

Working days and hours

Monday: 06:00/07:00 – 12:00/14:00Thursday: 06:00/07:00 – 12:00/14:00Sunday: 06:00/07:00 – 12:00/14:00

- You are a real hands-on person and enjoy physical work;
- You are physically fit and able to lift and move crates weighing up to 20 kg;
- You have no problem working with meat products;
- You are comfortable working in a refrigerated environment;
- You are able to work independently and take responsibility for your tasks;
- You are reliable and keep your commitments;
- You speak Dutch and/or English;
